--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,10 +6,23 @@ Searches the audit log.
 
 ```sh
 PYTHONPATH=src python -m auditlog.search --actor alice --action login
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m auditlog.search --actor alice --since 2026-01-01 --limit 20 --offset 20
 ```
 
-`--sort` and `--direction` select the ordering column and direction; both default
-to a timestamp descending sort. Results are unpaginated.
+Options:
 
-Clause building lives in `auditlog.filters`, so the same escaping and ordering
-rules apply to every query against the table.
+- `--actor` (required): exact actor to match.
+- `--action` (optional): exact action to match. Omit it to match every action for the actor.
+- `--since` (optional): ISO 8601 date or datetime (e.g. `2026-01-31`); only rows whose `ts` is
+  at or after it are returned.
+- `--sort`: any audit column (`id`, `actor`, `action`, `target`, `ts`); default `ts`.
+- `--direction`: `asc` or `desc`; default `desc`.
+- `--limit`: page size, 1 to 1000; default 50.
+- `--offset`: rows to skip; default 0.
+
+Ties are broken by `id` in the same direction, so pages are stable. Invalid values are rejected
+with a usage error.
+
+All filter values are bound as query parameters. Sort column and direction cannot be bound, so
+`auditlog.filters` validates them against allowlists; the same rules apply to every query against
+the table.
